{"fingerprint":"3691e1a9f41b5aee09fcae8c1fbbd91cda2ed35c61f98cb59182f9593102b4ab","path":"src/review_gauntlet/cli.py","rule_id":"data-validation","content":"The mark command accepts waiver metadata for every target state and stores it even when it is not semantically applicable. That lets `review-gauntlet mark RGF-0001 confirmed --until 2000-01-01` persist expiry metadata on a confirmed finding, and if the finding is later transitioned to waived without a fresh `--until`, expiry checks only inspect the latest waived/accepted-risk event and will treat the waiver as non-expiring. Validate `--until` (and owner expiry metadata) only for terminal waiver/risk states, or clear/reject it for other state transitions so stale metadata cannot influence later policy decisions.","suggestion_code":"def _cmd_mark(args: argparse.Namespace, store: SessionStore) -> None:
    mapping = {
        "confirmed": FindingState.CONFIRMED,
        "false-positive": FindingState.FALSE_POSITIVE,
        "waived": FindingState.WAIVED,
        "accepted-risk": FindingState.ACCEPTED_RISK,
        "fixed": FindingState.FIXED_PENDING_VERIFICATION,
    }
    metadata_states = {"waived", "accepted-risk"}
    if args.until and args.state not in metadata_states:
        raise ValueError("mark --until is only valid for waived or accepted-risk findings")
